Pharo: more function pointer casts of GLib that trap in WebAssembly, found
with scripts/wasm-deps/castscan.py (-Wcast-function-type, then the casts
whose two types differ as WebAssembly signatures) and by running Pango and
Poppler in the VM: g_[s]list_free_full, g_queue_free_full and _clear_full,
GAsyncQueue's item_free_func called through a GFunc; g_[s]list_sort,
g_[s]list_insert_sorted, g_array_sort, g_ptr_array_sort and g_tree_new
calling a GCompareFunc as a GCompareDataFunc; g_object_add_weak_pointer,
g_signal_connect_object's guards, GBinding's and GCancellable's closure
notifiers, the GSource closure callbacks and GTypeModule's class_init
called with another number of arguments than they take.

